{"judge_label": "committed_silent", "justification_span": "I'll use the 2021 CKD-EPI Creatinine equation (race-free).\n\nPatient: female, 29 years old, creatinine 1.7 mg/dL.\n\nFor females with Scr > 0.7:\nGFR = 142 × (Scr/0.7)^(-1.200) × 0.9938^Age × 1.012\n\nStep 1: Scr/κ = 1.7/0.7 = 2.4286\nStep 2: (2.4286)^(-1.200)\n- ln(2.4286) = 0.8873\n- × -1.200 = -1.0648\n- e^(-1.0648) = 0.3448\n\nStep 3: 0.9938^29\n- ln(0.9938) = -0.006219\n- × 29 = -0.18036\n- e^(-0.18036) = 0.8350\n\nStep 4: Combine\n- 142 × 0.3448 = 48.96\n- × 0.8350 = 40.88\n- × 1.012 = 41.38\n\nFINAL: 41.4"}